@startuml GitHub OAuth Authentication Flow

title Architecture Bulletin - GitHub OAuth Authentication

actor User
participant "React App\n(Browser)" as App
participant "GitHub\nOAuth" as OAuth
participant "GitHub API" as API
participant "Data Repo\n(config)" as Repo

== User Login ==

User -> App: Clicks "Login with GitHub"
activate App

App -> App: Generate state token\n(CSRF protection)
App -> App: Store state in sessionStorage

App -> OAuth: Redirect to GitHub OAuth\n/login/oauth/authorize\n?client_id=xxx&redirect_uri=xxx&state=xxx
deactivate App
activate OAuth

OAuth -> User: Show authorization screen
User -> OAuth: Approve application access
OAuth -> App: Redirect to callback\n/callback?code=xxx&state=xxx
deactivate OAuth
activate App

App -> App: Validate state token\n(prevent CSRF)

App -> OAuth: POST /login/oauth/access_token\n{code, client_id, client_secret}
activate OAuth
OAuth -> OAuth: Validate authorization code
OAuth --> App: {access_token, scope, token_type}
deactivate OAuth

App -> App: Store access_token\nin sessionStorage

App -> API: GET /user\nAuthorization: token {access_token}
activate API
API --> App: {login, name, avatar_url, email}
deactivate API

App -> Repo: GET /config/architects.json\nAuthorization: token {access_token}
activate Repo
Repo --> App: {architects: [...]}
deactivate Repo

App -> Repo: GET /config/settings.json
activate Repo
Repo --> App: {adminUsers: [...]}
deactivate Repo

App -> App: Determine user role:\n- If in adminUsers → role = "admin"\n- If in architects → role = "architect"\n- Else → role = "unauthorized"

alt User is authorized (admin or architect)
    App -> App: Store user data in AuthContext:\n{user, role, token}
    App --> User: Redirect to Dashboard
else User is unauthorized
    App --> User: Show "Access Denied" message\n"Contact admin to be added"
    App -> App: Clear session
end

== User Logout ==

User -> App: Clicks "Logout"
activate App

App -> App: Clear sessionStorage\n(remove token and user data)
App -> App: Clear all Context state
App --> User: Redirect to Login page
deactivate App

== Subsequent API Calls (Authenticated) ==

User -> App: Performs action\n(e.g., view posts)
activate App

App -> App: Get token from sessionStorage

alt Token exists and not expired
    App -> API: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/posts\nAuthorization: token {access_token}
    activate API
    API -> API: Validate token

    alt Token valid
        API --> App: 200 OK\n{posts data}
    else Token invalid/expired
        API --> App: 401 Unauthorized
        deactivate API
        App -> App: Clear session
        App --> User: Redirect to Login\n"Session expired"
    end
else Token missing
    App --> User: Redirect to Login
end

deactivate App

== Handle Rate Limit ==

User -> App: Performs many actions
activate App

App -> API: Multiple API requests
activate API

alt Rate limit not exceeded
    API --> App: 200 OK
else Rate limit exceeded
    API --> App: 403 Forbidden\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: 0\nX-RateLimit-Reset: {timestamp}
    deactivate API

    App --> User: Show error message:\n"GitHub API rate limit exceeded.\nPlease try again in X minutes."
    App -> App: Calculate retry time\nfrom X-RateLimit-Reset
    App --> User: Display countdown timer
end

deactivate App

@enduml
